{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788127284,"nonce":"xBzc2IRmTLFGAQsC3sm/Rd4Weu0=","message":"RESOLVED by Dorian — orchestrator, session 3. Unblocks this spec.\n\n**`rwa/` and `rwtest/` live in the autorimmer repo**, not in `rimworld-tools`.\nRecorded in DESIGN.md's decisions log; the Architecture diagram is updated too.\n\nRationale as chosen: the CLI is the client half of a protocol whose server half\nis in this repo, so a verb and its CLI surface change in one commit, one clone\ngives a working system, and rwtest asserts against `JOURNAL.md`, which is here.\nThe original split also had no review trail and no route to the second bench,\nsince `rimworld-tools` has no git at all.\n\n`rimworld-tools` stays exactly as it is — unversioned, reference-only. Nothing\ngets `git init`ed and nothing decompiled gets published.\n\n**For 2.5 specifically:** the PNG channel still REUSES `baseviz/`'s catalog and\ncanvas. That is a code-reuse dependency, not a location one — the new code lands\nin this repo and reads from `$RIMWORLD_TOOLS/baseviz/`. Whoever takes 2.5 should\ndecide import-vs-vendor and record it as an open-question resolution; vendoring\nis likely right, since an unversioned dependency cannot be pinned.\n\nThe spec bodies still say \"lives in rimworld-tools\". Treat this comment as the\namendment; do not follow the body on that point.","files":null}]}